From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:12:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] text: section navigator in the left side tools

View > Section navigator shows the sections of the current document as
a tree in the left side tools, like the navigator of word processors.
The section that contains the cursor is checked, and it and its
ancestors are bold. Clicking a section moves the cursor to its title.

"Levels" chooses how many levels are always shown; the branch that
contains the cursor is always expanded. The navigator stays open in new
windows and sessions (preference "section navigator").

Sections are found with tree-search-sections, as in Focus > Go to
section, and title strings are cached, so that an update costs a few
milliseconds on a document with 300 sections.
